From: PCI DirectPath Lab <lab@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-net-pci: add a lab-only class-code override

Expose the existing VirtIOPCIProxy class_code field on virtio-net-pci so a
black-box hypervisor experiment can hold the endpoint model, PCI identity,
capabilities, and topology constant while changing only the PCI base/subclass
code.  The zero default preserves normal QEMU behavior.

This is test instrumentation, not a proposed production option.
---
 hw/virtio/virtio-net-pci.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/virtio/virtio-net-pci.c b/hw/virtio/virtio-net-pci.c
--- a/hw/virtio/virtio-net-pci.c
+++ b/hw/virtio/virtio-net-pci.c
@@ -43,5 +43,7 @@ static Property virtio_net_properties[] = {
                     VIRTIO_PCI_FLAG_USE_IOEVENTFD_BIT, true),
     DEFINE_PROP_UINT32("vectors", VirtIOPCIProxy, nvectors,
                        DEV_NVECTORS_UNSPECIFIED),
+    DEFINE_PROP_UINT32("x-pci-class-code", VirtIOPCIProxy, class_code,
+                       0),
     DEFINE_PROP_END_OF_LIST(),
 };
--
2.43.0
